{#
  PRINT FOOTER — the provenance line at the end of a printed page.

  A sheet that has left the site has no address bar and no history: it needs to say
  where it came from and when it was taken, or it is an undated photocopy. Screen
  never shows it (see theme/_print.scss).

  The URL is rendered here as well as written by print-footer.js, so it survives with
  JS off. Craft's absoluteUrl is the right fallback — navigation on this site is real
  page loads, not pushState, so it cannot go stale.

  The DATE is deliberately NOT rendered here. It has to be the moment the page was
  PRINTED, and a server-rendered timestamp is the moment the page was rendered — which
  a template cache would make hours or days old, while claiming otherwise. Empty with
  JS off is honest; a wrong date is not.
#}
<div class="c-print-footer" data-print-footer>
    <p class="c-print-footer__label">Generated from:</p>
    <p class="c-print-footer__url" data-print-url>{{ craft.app.request.absoluteUrl }}</p>
    <p class="c-print-footer__date" data-print-date></p>
</div>
